<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<RomanProgram schemaVersion="28" APTVersion="Version 2025.8.1  JWST PRD: PRDAPTSOC-072-002, Roman PRD: RPRDDEVSOC-023" xmlns="http://www.stsci.edu/Roman/APT">
    <ProgramInformation>
        <ProgramPhase>Approved</ProgramPhase>
        <Title>CAR-170: Straylight From Sky</Title>
        <Abstract>This CAR scans the field of regard in pitch and roll to examine the susceptibility of RST to solar stray light. To stay at near constant galactic latitudes, the observations are split between the north and south CVZs. Each observation consists of a series of exposures with F062 (low out-of-band susceptibility, maximum in-band sensivitity) and the prism (maximum out-of-band sensitivity due to residual stray light leaks, and moderate in-band sensitivity), in a sequence that aims at minimizing the number of EWA moves. 

This CAR is DOY-dependent. The targets are constructed and position angles are constrained based on the starting date &amp; time of the whole sequence. This is essential to force the observatory to go to the desired roll angles.</Abstract>
        <ProgramID>105</ProgramID>
        <StsciEditNumber>1</StsciEditNumber>
        <ProgramCategory>COM</ProgramCategory>
        <ProgramCategorySubtype>WFI</ProgramCategorySubtype>
        <AllowRestricted>true</AllowRestricted>
        <IncludesCalibrations>false</IncludesCalibrations>
        <PureParallelProgram>false</PureParallelProgram>
        <Cycle>0</Cycle>
